return [
 'formula-1' => [
 'kicker' => 'Motorsport',
 'title' => 'Formula 1 - Beyond the Glitz, Glamour & Technical Innovations',
 'standfirst' => 'Fast cars and breakneck speeds. Exotic locations. Glitz and glamour. The best of the best. That’s arguably what Formula 1 is and it’s a sport that embodies both of these definitions of luxury effortlessly.',
        'byline' => 'Thiemo Albers-Daly',
        'role' => 'Award winning Freelance Motorsport Journalist and PR Consultant',
        'images' => [
            ['file' => 'Formula_1_Grand_Prix_Race_EBD_Magazine_2026.webp', 'alt' => 'Formula 1 cars racing at night beneath a large Heineken 0.0 sign.'],
            ['file' => 'Portrait_Wide_Thiemo_Albers-Daly_Motorsport_Journalist_EBD_Magazine_2026.webp', 'alt' => 'Thiemo Albers-Daly.'],
        ],
        'blocks' => [
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'Every year twenty-two of the world’s most elite racing drivers travel the globe to duke it out amongst themselves on a series of racetracks to determine that year’s World Champion. Teams, sponsors and industries, each of which are worth billions, support them and fight each other, and everyone else, for the privilege of doing so.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'Since its inception in 1950, F1 has been described as the pinnacle of motorsport. It still carries that moniker today but that definition has expanded far beyond the racetrack. For example, Grand Prix are now no longer just events; they are tailor made experiences.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'From the explosion of social media in the sport over the last decade to even driver customised Grandstands such as the Lewis Hamilton Grandstand in Las Vegas, there are so many layers to this access and customisation. That’s before we even get to merchandise.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'The cost involved, both monetarily and the time invested, is gigantic - much like every other scale on which you can measure F1. That goes from both being in the sport itself as well as being a fan at almost any level.'],
 ['type' => 'quote', 'text' => '“A lot of people criticize Formula 1 as an unnecessary risk. But what would life be like if we only did what is necessary?” - Nika Lauda, F1 World Champion 1975, 1977 and 1984'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'If it was just F1 that was guilty of this, there would certainly be more of a conversation to be had about its place in the world. But the same could be said for any other sport.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'So F1 is most certainly a luxury and like sustainability, both are continuously evolving. This goes hand in hand with F1 - both on and off track.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'Look at Drive to Survive. A blend between a docuseries and reality TV, it has introduced F1 to a brand new fanbase and made this luxury item accessible for millions of people around the world. It has brought the sport into every corner of their everyday lives. This is reinforced by social media and the understanding by teams and drivers that they must engage with these forms of communication if they are to sustain themselves and thrive.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'On track, the cars are continuously subjected to endless rules and regulations that can and do change year upon year - all in the pursuit of perfection. The knowledge and technology garnered from this filters back through to everyday use, such as improving crash structures of vehicles and the development of more effective medical equipment, such as a new breathing aid developed by Mercedes during the Covid Pandemic.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'Those working behind the scenes have seen the value in sharing their insights and experiences. Consequently, they provide the fans with a seemingly endless amount of information, through books, podcasts, reels, etc. When almost a century of history meets the communication technology and consumability of the twenty-first century, a symbiotic match is made that creates a sustainable loop.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'Consequently, F1 is now in a position where it’s more accessible than ever while remaining unobtainable in many ways for the masses. Subscriptions to watch it aren’t cheap and neither are ticket prices, even at the most basic level. Yet more often than not, Grand Prix weekends are attended by a sell out crowd who the sport has convinced that the cost involved is worth it. Other series may be cheaper and they may provide more straightforward value for money but they all lack one fundamental and obvious thing - they’re not F1.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'Formula 1 is undoubtedly at an all time high right now. As with anything, that will end at some point. But how it ends - or simply evolves as it always has done - will inform us of what sustainability looks like for F1 and how that ties into the overall longevity of the sport.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'Formula 1 has already become more sustainable and that can be assessed in a number of ways too. The chronological ordering of the Championship, for example, has been altered in recent years to reduce the environmental impact that the sport has. This has been coupled with the use of reduced emissions in transport and the increased use of biofuel. In 2024, Mercedes used HVO100 biofuel for the European portion of their season, achieving 98% coverage in race and marketing trucks and generators, and saving more than 500 tonnes of CO2e. This isn’t just happening in Formula 1 but in its junior series and other international series too. F1 is a sport that has always prided itself on pushing the boundaries of what is possible too with regards to technology. The advancements made there can often be seen in everyday road cars, such as with hybrid powertrains and active suspension.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'Formula 1 is also becoming more inclusive and this is one of the few sports building this firmly into the future of the sport.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'Women in Motorsport have been on the rise in recent years - both on the track and behind the scenes. This isn’t just the case in F1 either - it encompasses the entire racing world across the globe. F1 Academy, an all-female junior racing series, was conceived with the notion of providing more young women with the opportunities and visibility needed to continue in the sport. Extreme H sees male and female drivers competing on an equal playing field. Formula 2, Formula 3 and IndyCar have all redesigned their cars to better accommodate all body types, rather than just men. Behind the scenes, the interest in STEM subjects from women has risen markedly and in a series such as Formula E, the majority of the public facing communications roles are filled by women.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'The increased interest in F1 has seeped out into every corner of the motorsport world and with it, you can glimpse what the future will look like.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'With more brands, companies and sponsors becoming interested in F1’s orbit too, the opportunity for brand new avenues to explore continues to expand too. Look at the role of fashion in F1 today.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'Each Grand Prix weekend feels like some kind of a catwalk, either thanks to Lewis Hamilton or other drivers on the grid - just look at drivers like Yuki Tsunoda and Zhou Guanyu as past examples of this. Then there’s also the role that the driver’s partners play, as well as the celebrities in attendance, and the interest that they all generate from a previously untapped portion of the fanbase that the sport perhaps didn’t even realise that it could appeal to. F1 teams have individual clothing brands and Tommy Hilfiger even fielded a car in F1 Academy for two years.'],
 ['type' => 'quote', 'text' => '“In F1, I felt like an outcast. In fashion, I felt like I belonged.” - Lewis Hamilton'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'F1 is an intense and addictive luxury. It always has been and always should be. Luxury is a core part of its identity and part of what makes it special. But that doesn’t mean it should be a luxury that only some of us can enjoy, in whatever form that might take. Be it from a fan watching at home, to attending a Grand Prix, to working behind the scenes to being a competitor - it should all be attainable but through the right methodology. It’s arguably always been a sustainable luxury but the definition of what that means has evolved and F1 has moved with that. When you dig into the details, how that is actually the case becomes clearer.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'Is Formula 1 a luxury? Of course it is. If it wasn’t, it wouldn’t have survived for the last seventy-six years. However, its definition of luxury may simply challenge your notions and perspective of what that means.'],
 ],
 ],
 'family-values' => [
 'kicker' => 'Family',
 'title' => 'Putting Family Values into Practice',
 'standfirst' => 'At the end of a family retreat, the values cards go back in their box. Integrity. Legacy. Generosity. Stewardship. Someone photographs the wall of sticky notes. The family leaves with a Vision statement everyone recognizes as its own.',
 'byline' => 'Dr. Stacy Feiner',
 'role' => '',
 'blocks' => [
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'Eight months later, those values face a test. The trustees meet to consider a request from a 34-year-old daughter. She has left the family company to build an organic, regenerative farm, an expression of the family\'s commitment to stewardship. She has also helped design and patent the irrigation system that the farm will be a test site for. Now she is asking for an early distribution from her trust. The trustees review the trust instrument, distribution policy, their obligations to all beneficiaries, and a memo about liquidity. That same afternoon, they decline her request stating it appears to be an exception, and out of scope.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'The daughter is the first to experience the gap between what the family says it values and how decisions are made. But the implications reach beyond her request. What does the decision say about the family\'s understanding of stewardship? Is there room for a family member to express a shared value in a different way? And what do other family members learn from the response? A family\'s values are tested not when everyone agrees with them, but when someone acts on them in a way the family didn\'t anticipate.'],
 ['type' => 'h2', 'text' => 'Values have to show up in family life'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'Families invest time in retreats, develop shared language, and create statements about the kind of family they want to be. They also create trusts, policies, councils, and other structures to manage their wealth. Too often, these efforts operate separately. Conversations about values happen at one time; decisions about money, authority, and individual opportunity happen at another.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'A Vision statement isn\'t useful simply because it exists. Its meaning emerges in how family members treat one another, how they exercise authority, and how they respond when someone takes an unexpected path. This is not to say that every individual choice must be supported financially or that shared values require everyone to agree. The trustees may have sound fiduciary reasons to decline the daughter\'s request. They must consider the trust\'s terms, financial realities, and the interests of every beneficiary. But those responsibilities do not relieve them of the need to understand the family they serve.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'Trustees have an ongoing responsibility to stay informed about the family\'s circumstances, priorities, and intentions. They should know about the retreat, understand what came out of it, and keep that understanding current. They cannot assume that administering the documents alone is enough. Their decisions are part of the family\'s life, and they should be made with an awareness of what the family is trying to build. The family, in turn, has a responsibility to connect its stated values to the structures and decisions that shape its future.'],
 ['type' => 'h2', 'text' => 'Making room for different paths'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'An Ethic of Care offers a useful way to think about what this requires. At its simplest, care means understanding people\'s circumstances, considering how decisions affect them and others, and paying attention to their needs and expectations. Here, that begins with taking the daughter\'s work seriously. Why does she see the farm as an expression of stewardship? What has she built? How does her idea fit—or challenge—the family\'s understanding of its purpose?'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'It also means considering the other beneficiaries and the long-term health of the trust. The trustees might explore alternatives to an early distribution, such as a loan or staged arrangement, if permitted. They may conclude that none is appropriate. The point is not to guarantee a particular outcome. It is to make room for a thoughtful conversation in which the daughter\'s initiative, the family\'s values, and the trustees\' obligations are all taken seriously.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'Care is relational. It supports belonging to shared ideals while making room for individual agency and self-expression. It recognizes that people can share a sense of purpose without choosing identical ways to live it. The daughter\'s younger brother is watching, too. He sees what happens when his sister takes an independent path and asks the family to consider it. He begins adjusting his own plans to fit what he believes the family will approve. No one has told him to do that. He has drawn his own conclusions.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'That is how a family teaches its next generation. Not only through its Vision statement or what it says at a retreat, but through the everyday exercise of authority and the way it responds when someone challenges familiar expectations. A decision about one beneficiary can influence what others believe is possible for themselvesA family can say it values stewardship, initiative, and independent thinking. But those values have to leave room for people to interpret and express them in different ways. Otherwise, the family may unintentionally teach that belonging depends on following an established path.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'The daughter may still be told no. The trust may not be able to support her request. But she and her brother should be able to see that her work was understood, that the family\'s values were part of the deliberation, and that a different path does not put her place in the family in question. Putting family values into practice does not mean making every decision come out the way someone hopes. It means making decisions in a way that reflects what the family says matters—and recognizing that those decisions shape the family that comes next.'],
 ],
 ],
 'extraordinary-difference' => [
 'kicker' => 'Impact',
 'title' => 'The Greatest Myth About Luxury? That Making an Extraordinary Difference Is Reserved for the Few.',
 'standfirst' => 'What if life\'s greatest luxury is the power we already have to change lives, create possibilities, and leave a meaningful legacy?',
 'byline' => 'Priscilla Stephan',
 'role' => '',
 'blocks' => [
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'Think about someone who\'s made a meaningful difference in your life.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'Perhaps they challenged an assumption that was holding you back, stood by their principles when it wasn\'t easy, or helped you recognize a strength you hadn\'t seen in yourself.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'What stays with you isn\'t necessarily what they owned or achieved. It\'s what became possible because they were there.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'What if we\'re overlooking one of life\'s greatest luxuries: our ability to make a meaningful difference right now?'],
 ['type' => 'h2', 'text' => 'What if luxury could mean more?'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'Luxury often brings to mind exquisite craftsmanship, beautiful possessions, exceptional experiences, and the freedom to enjoy life\'s finer pleasures.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'And why not? It\'s wonderful to want beautiful things, pursue ambitious dreams, and enjoy abundance.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'But perhaps luxury can also mean having the freedom to live by our values, choose what matters, and contribute in ways that feel deeply meaningful.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'A rich life can encompass what we have, what we create, and what we give of ourselves.'],
 ['type' => 'h2', 'text' => 'Are we waiting for permission we don\'t need?'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'We often attach conditions to making an impact:'],
 ['type' => 'quote', 'text' => '“When I have more money, I\'ll give back.”'],
 ['type' => 'quote', 'text' => '“When I have more time, I\'ll get involved.”'],
 ['type' => 'quote', 'text' => '“When I have another degree, I\'ll have something valuable to offer.”'],
 ['type' => 'quote', 'text' => '“When I have more influence, I\'ll make a real difference.”'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'Or: *“I\'m only one person. What can I possibly change?”*'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'Resources, expertise, and influence can expand our reach. Some ambitions require them. But what if we\'ve confused what helps us scale our impact with what gives us permission to begin?'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'And what if we\'re measuring our contribution only by what\'s visible, impressive, or easily counted?'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'Not every meaningful difference comes with applause, a title, or a measurable result.'],
 ['type' => 'h2', 'text' => 'The impact we rarely see'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'In my work with accomplished leaders and entrepreneurs, I\'ve learned that success and fulfillment aren\'t always the same thing. Even after remarkable achievements, people can feel called to contribute in new ways.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'That longing isn\'t reserved for the wealthy or influential. It\'s human.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'Impact can look like asking the question that changes how a team approaches a challenge. Giving someone room to develop their own voice. Or choosing integrity when a shortcut would be easier.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'A leader who consistently models respect can shape a culture where others do the same. One choice can influence many more.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'The significance of our impact isn\'t always determined by its size, but by what it makes possible.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'And sometimes our greatest influence comes not from a deliberate act of service, but from who we\'re being in our everyday lives.'],
 ['type' => 'h2', 'text' => 'It\'s not either/or. It\'s yes, AND.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'Recognizing our everyday impact isn\'t an invitation to think smaller, abandon ambition, or settle for less.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'Quite the opposite. It\'s an opportunity to value a dimension of our contribution we may barely notice.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'You get to be intentional about who you\'re being and the difference you make each day.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'AND you get to dream big, build extraordinary things, champion causes, and create change on a much larger scale.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'AND you get to enjoy the wealth, beauty, freedom, and experiences that make life fulfilling for you.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'These possibilities reinforce one another. The way we live can give deeper meaning to what we create—and to what we enjoy.'],
 ['type' => 'h2', 'text' => 'Three questions to make your impact more intentional:'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => '1. Who do I want to be in the lives of the people I touch?'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'Courageous? Generous? Curious? Encouraging? Choose one quality to embody in a conversation today.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => '2. What can I contribute with what I already have?'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'Perhaps you can share an insight, speak up for a better way of doing things, or make space for someone else\'s ideas. Choose one action and take it.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => '3. What evidence of my impact am I overlooking?'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'For the next seven days, notice moments when your choices reflect your values, even if nobody comments. You may be contributing more than you realize.'],
 ['type' => 'h2', 'text' => 'A rich legacy begins now'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'I believe legacy is too important to leave until the end of our lives.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'It isn\'t only the wealth we pass down, the institutions we build, or the achievements beside our names. It\'s also the confidence we awaken, the standards we model, and the possibilities that continue because we were here.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'Redefining luxury doesn\'t ask us to want less. It invites us to recognize more of what makes life rich.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'We can create a life we love, pursue extraordinary possibilities, and make a difference along the way.'],
 ['type' => 'h2', 'text' => 'Because the richest legacy isn\'t simply measured by what we accumulate or accomplish, but by the lives we enrich, the possibilities we create, and the difference we choose to make starting today.'],
 ['type' => 'h2', 'text' => 'About the Author'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'Priscilla Stephan helps accomplished founders and visionary leaders discover what truly matters, navigate pivotal transitions, and turn their success into meaningful impact. As founder of Pinnacle Purpose® and author of the Soulfluent® Leadership Business Guide, she combines strategic insight and intuitive guidance to help her clients create fulfilling next chapters and lasting legacies. You can learn more at www.pinnaclepurpose.com'],
 ],
 ],
 'freedom-to-choose' => [
 'kicker' => 'Wealth',
 'title' => 'What If the Greatest Luxury Is The Freedom to Choose?',
 'standfirst' => 'On wealth, family expectations and the future we make possible.',
 'byline' => 'Ildiko Markus',
 'role' => 'Founder, Ildiko Markus Advisory',
 'blocks' => [
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'There are families doing extraordinary things with their wealth. They\'re supporting medical breakthroughs, investing in cleaner technologies and giving promising businesses the chance to grow. I find that genuinely encouraging.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'Yet there\'s something about this that deserves a closer look. When someone has the means to make almost any choice, how free do they actually feel to make it?'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'A family business might have supported a community for forty years. The next generation could see a way to modernise it, improve its environmental practices or take it into a new market. They may have the resources, the expertise and the authority to do so.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'But what if changing direction feels like questioning everything their parents worked for?'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'Or take a woman who has sold the company she spent twenty years building. She has earned the freedom to decide what comes next. Perhaps she wants to back other founders, explore philanthropy or spend more time with her children. Yet she might find herself planning the next big achievement before she\'s even had a chance to ask what she wants now.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'Neither person necessarily needs to make a different decision. But how much do they really understand about what\'s influencing the one they\'re about to make?'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'Family loyalty can be a beautiful thing. So can ambition. The difficulty comes when an expectation we\'ve carried for years starts to feel like an obligation we never consciously chose.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'This is what I notice in my advisory work: the patterns beneath apparently straightforward decisions. The daughter who feels she must preserve a family tradition. The founder who can\'t quite separate her identity from the business. The person who has always been relied upon to do the sensible thing, even when something else matters deeply to them.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'These aren\'t reasons to dismiss good financial or legal advice. Quite the opposite. When someone understands what they want their wealth to achieve, their advisors are better placed to help them work out how to achieve it.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'And I don\'t believe the answer is always change. Sometimes keeping a business in the family is exactly right. Sometimes starting another company is a genuine joy. The point is being able to recognise the difference between a choice that feels right and one that simply feels expected.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'As a mother of two, I think about what we leave our children. Of course I want them to have security and opportunity. But I also want them to feel free to question what they\'ve inherited, including my own ideas about what a good life should look like.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'We talk about luxury in terms of beautiful places, exceptional experiences and the freedom wealth can buy. I appreciate all of that. Yet perhaps one of its greatest privileges is the freedom to decide what truly matters to us, even when that choice surprises the people closest to us.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'The legacy worth leaving goes beyond wealth carefully preserved. It\'s the freedom to make something of it that is genuinely our own.'],
 ],
 ],
 'orveda' => [
 'kicker' => 'Beauty Editor\'s Pick',
 'title' => 'Orveda: The Green Beauty Brand Worth Stopping For',
 'standfirst' => 'Exclusive to Harrods, Orveda combines biotechnology, vegan formulations and a skin-first philosophy in a collection that prioritises radiance, hydration and long-term skin health. As a makeup artist, these are the facial treatments and hero products that stood out to me.',
        'byline' => 'Viorela Coman',
        'role' => 'Beauty Editor',
        'images' => [
            ['file' => 'Packshot_Orveda_Omnipotent_Concentrate_EBD_Magazine_2026.webp', 'alt' => 'Orveda Omnipotent Concentrate bottle.'],
            ['file' => 'Packshot_Orveda_Bio-Tech_Emulsion_EBD_Magazine_2026.webp', 'alt' => 'Orveda Bio-Tech Emulsion bottle.'],
            ['file' => 'Packshot_Orveda_Healing_Sap_EBD_Magazine_2026.webp', 'alt' => 'Orveda Healing Sap bottle.'],
        ],
        'blocks' => [
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'As a beauty editor and makeup artist, I\'m always intrigued by brands that challenge conventional beauty thinking. While many skincare launches continue to focus on correcting, resurfacing and reversing, Orveda takes a noticeably different approach. Founded by beauty industry veterans Sue Nabi and Nicolas Vu, the French luxury skincare brand is built around the concept of skin longevity, focusing on resilience, vitality and working with the skin rather than against it.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'At its core, Orveda is a brand built around skin longevity. Combining biotech innovation, vegan formulations and a respect for the skin barrier, it takes a notably different approach from many performance-led skincare brands.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'What stood out to me wasn\'t a single hero product or headline-grabbing ingredient, but the brand\'s broader philosophy. Every formula and treatment is designed to work with the skin, focusing on hydration, resilience and radiance rather than aggressive correction.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'The facial experiences follow the same thinking. Tailored to individual skin needs, they focus on restoring balance and supporting healthy skin function. It\'s a subtle but important distinction, and one that reflects a wider movement towards thoughtful, preventative skincare rather than chasing instant transformations.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'During a recent visit to the Orveda space at Harrods, I experienced this philosophy first-hand. The Harrods team guides guests through a range of facial experiences, whether the goal is restoring luminosity, replenishing hydration or simply taking time to reset. It\'s a refreshing reminder that effective skincare isn\'t always about adding more products or more steps. Sometimes it\'s about understanding what the skin needs and responding accordingly.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'From a makeup artist\'s perspective, this approach makes complete sense. Healthy, balanced skin reflects light more beautifully, requires less coverage and allows complexion products to perform at their best. No amount of foundation can truly recreate the radiance of well-hydrated skin.'],
 ['type' => 'h2', 'text' => 'My Top Three Products from the Range'],
 ['type' => 'h3', 'text' => 'The Omnipotent Concentrate'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'If I had to choose a single hero product, this would be it. It gives the skin a fresher, more rested appearance and delivers the subtle plumpness and luminosity that makeup artists are often trying to create with strategic highlighting and expert skin preparation.'],
 ['type' => 'h3', 'text' => 'The Bio-Tech Emulsion'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'A lightweight moisturiser that delivers lasting hydration without feeling heavy. I particularly enjoyed it as a pre-makeup step because it creates a comfortable, balanced base while allowing the skin\'s natural glow to shine through.'],
 ['type' => 'h3', 'text' => 'The Healing Sap'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'It\'s the formula most closely associated with the brand: this essence-serum hybrid focuses on hydration, balance and skin vitality. It\'s easy to see why it has developed such a loyal following among those who prefer healthy-looking skin over dramatic overnight transformations.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'What I found most compelling about Orveda wasn\'t a single product or miracle claim, but the consistency of its philosophy. Across both treatments and formulations, the focus remains the same: supporting the skin\'s natural functions, strengthening resilience and encouraging long-term skin wellness rather than chasing quick fixes.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'For anyone interested in vegan luxury beauty, green innovation and facial treatments that prioritise skin wellness, Orveda offers an interesting alternative to more traditional luxury skincare brands.'],
 ['type' => 'h2', 'text' => 'Beauty Editor\'s Verdict'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'Orveda represents the future-facing side of luxury beauty: biotechnology meets sustainability, and high-performance skincare meets skin compatibility.'],
 ['type' => 'p', 'text' => 'If you\'re in London, do make time for a facial consultation and discover why this French green biotech brand has become one of my most interesting skincare discoveries this year. Sometimes the most effective beauty routine isn\'t about adding more steps. It\'s about choosing products that help your skin perform at its best.'],
 ],
 ],
